Now, let's go through the change request for approvals

We’ll review one change request at a time. For each, you can approve, approve with changes, defer or reject. Approval adds it to the implementation backlog; it does not activate payments or live trading.

Order	Change request
1	CR-001: Accounts, Security & Profiles
2	CR-002: Private Local Data, Bot Files & Exports
3	CR-003: Bot Store & Seller Commissions
4	CR-004: Memberships, Usage Limits & Leaderboards
5	CR-005: Membership Referrals & Commission Payouts

CR-001 — Accounts, Security & Profiles

The proposed scope is:

Feature	Behavior for approval
Registration	Verified email/password, Google sign-in or GitHub sign-in
Account recovery	Password reset and email verification through expiring, single-use links
Two-factor authentication	Authenticator app with recovery codes; optional for demo, required before live trading and designated sensitive actions
Profile personalization	Edit avatar, display name and unique username during an active session
Account linking	Connect additional sign-in methods after authenticating the existing account
User separation	Account ownership checks protect private settings, bots, history and Deriv connections
Developer testing	Startup-controlled authentication bypass using a separate test identity; visible development indicator; live trading blocked
Production protection	Authentication bypass cannot run in production
Session handling	Secure login/logout; session expiry cannot erase or transfer responsibility for existing broker positions

Google sign-in requests identity access only. GitHub sign-in does not request repository access.

Proposed priority: High—implement the account foundation before the multi-user Bot Manager, memberships and store. Final version numbering will follow this approval review.

Acceptance: Registration, verification, recovery, profile editing and two-factor flows work; cross-user access is denied; developer bypass cannot enable live trading or production access.

Do you approve CR-001 as described, approve with changes, defer it or reject it?

approve with one addition - the user should be able to enter and update their contact information, and choose their country/region. They should also have the option to disable if they want to be displayed on the leader board for their custom bots performance.

CR-001 is approved with your additions and recorded:

Users can enter and update contact information.
Users can select and update their country/region.
Users can disable public leaderboard display of their custom-bot performance.

Contact details remain private. The leaderboard preference will control public entries without deleting private performance history. I recommend leaderboard visibility off by default; that default remains proposed.

Next: CR-002 — Private Local Data, Bot Files & Exports

Feature	Behavior for approval
Local history	Automatically retain private, account-separated trading/training history on the device—your previously confirmed Option A
Data downloads	Export retained account data for selected dates, markets and modes as CSV or XLSX, including an active-session snapshot
Personal bot files	Import and export full bots, configurations and learned updates
Save/discard	At trading/training session end, offer saving a new bot version or discarding bot changes; discarding preserves trading history
File location	Use normal browser downloads, or a supported user-authorized file/folder picker
Server preferences	Explicitly saved market configurations persist separately from local bot files
Public bots	Only admins publish or update the public catalog; customizing one creates a private copy
Recovery	Automatically retain a minimal local journal of cycle protections and pending/open orders so crashes or discarded changes cannot reset trading obligations
Privacy	Exports exclude credentials and live-capital authorization; private training runs locally or through the local Python application
Retention controls	Provide local-storage usage, deletion controls and clear warnings that deleted or unavailable history cannot be exported

Server boundary: Authentication, profiles, security records and saved market preferences remain server-side. Store assets, subscriptions, commissions and leaderboard submissions require their separately approved server records.

Closing a browser cannot reliably trigger a save prompt, so the app will provide an explicit End Session action. Signing in elsewhere retrieves server preferences, not private files left on another device.

Proposed priority: High—establish this before expanding Bot Manager, training and portable files. Any download/upload quotas will be reviewed under CR-004.

Acceptance: Account separation works; exports match retained records and selected dates; save/discard behaves correctly; restarting preserves risk controls and order reconciliation.

Do you approve CR-002 as described, approve with changes, defer it or reject it?

approve

CR-002 is approved and recorded. CR-001 and CR-002 are now approved for implementation; neither has been implemented yet.

Next: CR-003 — Bot Store & Seller Commissions

Feature	Scope for approval
Create a listing	Available during an active trading session; capture an immutable copy of the current custom bot and configuration
Automated product details	Include market, bot version, market-condition snapshot, calculated win rate, sample size, demo/live source, period, profit and measured drawdown
Seller inputs	Set price between US$30–$50 and add descriptive text; cannot manually replace calculated statistics
Private paid products	Store the listed package on the server; require purchase entitlement to access it
Seller commission	80% of net sale price; business receives the remaining 20% of that same base
Purchased bots	Show compatible purchases in the market’s bot selector; allow private nicknames and descriptions
Customer results	Preview and publish session statistics with comments; distinguish original and customized versions and demo/live results
Store discovery	Categorize and filter by market, bot type, price, training status and performance evidence
Public-bot restrictions	Unmodified members-only public bots offer no download or resale action
Licensing	A custom bot’s download/resale availability remains subject to ownership and derivative-use permissions
Shared-bot updates	Automatically collect candidates, then publish only after weekly admin approval
Version protection	Existing sessions retain their selected version; published updates do not silently alter running bots

Recommended decisions to complete this request

Listing eligibility: Allow both live-price demo and real-money sessions, clearly labelled. Offline simulated results cannot be presented as market-trading evidence.
Net sale price: Define it as the actual sale amount excluding taxes, less payment-processing fees and applicable refunds/chargebacks. Show each deduction in the seller’s ledger.
Paid-bot updates: Require admin review before publication. Customers retain their purchased version and explicitly choose whether to install an approved update.
Private purchase labels: Store nicknames/descriptions as private account preferences so they follow the buyer across devices.
Payout rules: Finalize seller payout timing, minimums and refund handling alongside the payment system. The membership commission schedule does not automatically apply to store sales.

Publishing a listing explicitly uploads that bot package. Posting results uploads the selected performance summary—not unrelated private history or credentials. Published win rates describe recorded results and do not promise future performance.

Proposed placement: Expand the existing marketplace release after accounts, bot versioning, performance records and purchase entitlements are ready.

Acceptance: Listings preserve the correct bot version; purchases enforce access; commission calculations reconcile; public-bot restrictions work; reports cannot double-count trades; updates require approval.

Do you approve CR-003, including the five recommended decisions above, approve with changes, defer it or reject it?

approved

