Next: CR-004 — Memberships, Usage Limits & Leaderboards

Account type	Access and allowances
Guest	Basic public bots in demo only; no customization, custom-file uploads or live trading; expires after one hour without interaction
Registered free	Basic public bots, customization and building bots; live trading requires separate authorization; two trading days monthly
Subscriber	Free-account features plus members-only public bots, membership badge and unlimited custom-bot/configuration uploads/downloads
All registered users	Unlimited access/export of locally retained trading data

Basic public bots undergo training no more than annually. Members-only public bots receive approved updates through the weekly review process.

Subscription	Total monthly account-wide trading days
Bronze	7
Silver	14
Gold	21
Platinum	28

These allowances are shared across markets and cycles and do not roll over. Subscription prices remain undecided.

Usage rules proposed for approval

Free accounts receive one combined bot/configuration download per trading market per day, and one combined upload daily across all markets.
Additional bot/configuration operations cost US$2.50 each, after included allowances are used. Subscribers incur no such charges.
Trading-data exports remain unlimited and uncharged. I recommend treating raw CSV training-data imports separately from paid bot/configuration imports.
Failed operations and retries do not produce duplicate charges.
Quotas, payments and permissions are enforced on the server; the browser displays remaining allowances.
Uploaded working bots do not automatically persist across sessions. Re-upload uses an available allowance or paid operation; retained local history remains intact.
Additional trading days cost US$0.50 each, purchased in blocks of at least two days.

Recommended day-accounting decisions

Reset allowances on the 1st of each month, Jamaica time, including annual subscribers.
Use one active account-wide cycle covering all selected markets; five simultaneous markets consume the same cycle days.
Reserve planned days at cycle start. Cancellation consumes at least one day, rounded up by elapsed 24-hour periods: 29 hours consumes two days. Release unused reservations.
Extra days expire at month-end and do not roll over. A cycle must fit the remaining days before that reset; purchased days can extend its available duration within that boundary.
Login expiry does not restart a cycle or reset risk controls. Exhausted allowances stop new entries while outstanding positions remain managed.

Leaderboard and titles

The proposed scope includes named public bots and consenting users’ custom bots, market-specific titles, multiple titles per user, and filters for market, country/region and sale status.

For consistent qualification, I recommend:

At least 90% win rate, inclusive.
A separate minimum of 500 eligible settled forward-demo or live trades for the exact bot/configuration version and market—not merely 500 training records.
Separate demo/live rankings and public/custom-bot categories.
Display sample size, evaluation period, net profit, drawdown and evidence level.
Preserve historical achievements while distinguishing them from current performance.
Honor the CR-001 visibility preference; recommend off by default.
Compare shared-bot candidates on compatible evaluation data before weekly admin approval; a higher percentage alone does not trigger publication.

These thresholds qualify a recorded achievement, not a profitability or safety guarantee.

Proposed placement: Build entitlements before paid usage; add leaderboards after reliable version-specific performance records. Membership prices remain a separate decision.

