Final review: CR-005 — Membership Referrals & Commission Payouts

Feature	Scope for approval
Referral model	Direct referrals only initially; automatic assignment deferred
Eligible referrers	Active subscribed members, preserving your requested eligibility rule
Commission	25% of gross membership fees; no commission on store purchases or usage top-ups
Monthly billing	Renewals due on the 1st
Grace period	Through 11:59 PM on the 5th, Jamaica time; inactive from the 6th if unpaid
Commission payment	Prior-month commissions released and payouts initiated on the 5th of the following month
Annual membership	Commission vests monthly using the actual annual subscription price
Dashboard	Referral link, QR, code, referred usernames/count, expected earnings, pending/available balances and payout history
Withdrawals	Requested withdrawals or automatic payouts to a verified, supported destination
Missing destination	Available commission remains recorded as owed until a destination is verified

Recommended rules included for approval

Gross calculation: Use the subscription amount actually charged after discounts, before processing fees, excluding separately collected taxes. Refunds reduce commission proportionately. A $240 annual subscription produces $60 total commission, vesting at $5 per service month.
Late-payment eligibility: Missing the grace deadline forfeits that month’s unvested referral commission. Late payment restores membership access, but commission eligibility resumes in the next qualifying month. Previously earned commissions remain payable.
Midmonth registration: Prorate the first subscription month. New referrers qualify from paid activation for that initial month; they cannot earn on earlier transactions.
Annual status: Annual subscribers remain active throughout their prepaid term. Allocate monthly vesting to the applicable service periods, with documented rounding and partial-month handling.
Refund protection: Hold disputed commissions, reverse commissions attributable to refunds/chargebacks, and offset disclosed reversals against future earnings. Maintain a business reserve for exposure after payout.
Attribution: One direct referrer per subscriber, fixed at first paid activation. Show the selected referrer before confirmation; prevent self-referrals and duplicate-account abuse.
Financial records: Maintain an authoritative server-side commission ledger. Browser deletion, logout or inactivity cannot erase earned balances.
Payout scope: Start with commission accounting and disbursements—not deposits, transfers between users or custody of trading funds. Finalize provider, supported countries/currencies, minimums and fees before launch.

Launch condition: Subscriber-only earning eligibility remains subject to qualified legal review and payment-provider acceptance. Free affiliate enrollment remains an alternative for later consideration; it is not silently substituted into this request.

Proposed placement: After subscriptions, identity verification and payment reconciliation. Bank arrival times may follow the payout initiation date.

Acceptance: Accurate attribution, gross-fee calculations, monthly vesting, inactivity handling, refund adjustments and reconciled payouts, with no duplicate payments.

