A channel can contain both paid native videos and free external videos. Its paid subscription must never block access to those external videos.

External integration is possible, within platform limits

YouTube supports embedded players and playlists; its channel metadata can support listing channel uploads. TikTok supports video and creator-profile embeds. Instagram supports public-content embedding. These integrations do not automatically synchronize external likes, comments or subscribers.

Unavailable, deleted or private content will need an appropriate fallback. Linked content will retain its source attribution.

