version 1.1 report - The market observation graph need data labels and horizontal axis label. Also, it needs a way to override the pause once floor is reached. The user should be able to manually confirm over-riding the floor to restart with new balance and calculated floor for new set capital. Also, individual capital should be assigned for each marketplace trader initialized.

Recorded your v1.1 testing feedback as changes requested.

1. Observation graph — correction for v1.2

Add price/data labels, a horizontal-axis label, and readable time ticks with timezone. Existing observations without timestamps must be labelled honestly rather than assigned invented times.

2. Floor-stop restart — proposed behavior

When a trader reaches its floor:

Stop new entries and reconcile outstanding orders.
Offer “Restart with new capital.”
Show available balance, requested allocation, recalculated floor and new loss allowance.
Require explicit confirmation.
Preserve the previous run’s losses and floor in history.

The old floor remains unchanged; the newly authorized run receives its own floor.

Repeated resets increase cumulative risk: $50 stopping at $40, then restarting that $40 with a $32 floor, permits a total loss of $18, exceeding the original $10 allowance.

3. Individual market allocations — proposed behavior

Each initialized market trader gets its own capital allocation, balance, floor, profit targets and trading status. Combined allocations cannot exceed available account funds. One market reaching its floor pauses that trader.

Monthly trading-day allowances remain account-wide; restarting capital does not replenish days.

The reset and per-market allocations change the approved risk model. Under your change-control instruction, please confirm adding these as CR-009 to v1.2. The chart correction is already recorded.

