If i want to change the business logo or name, can that be done via the content management section asic account information:

SELECT id, username, role, plan, status FROM users;

Avoid manually changing balances, floors, orders or permissions—those changes can break the app’s protections and accounting.

i want to view datasets as tables in vs code

Yes—you can browse the app’s SQLite datasets as tables inside VS Code.

Open Extensions with Ctrl+Shift+X.
Search for SQLite Viewer and install SQLite Viewer by Florian Klampfer.
Open your extracted BotForge27 folder in VS Code.
In the Explorer, click a database:
pilot-data/platform.sqlite3 — accounts, settings, reviews and business records.
pilot-data/private/<account-id>/sandbox.sqlite3 — trading data.
For public-feed sessions, look inside pilot-public-data/.
Select a table in the viewer to browse its rows and columns.

Start with these tables:

Table	Contents
users	Test accounts and roles
trades	Retained trading records
records	Bots, configurations and other application records; details are in the JSON body column
reviews	Checklist decisions and feedback
audit	Recorded actions
quota	Monthly day usage

Use the viewer’s read-only mode to inspect the data without changing it.